<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	`ighostvt-cli` on the device.

	Two keys, and they are the whole of its privilege: the marker the daemon
	authenticates against (`PeerAuthenticator` also requires the caller to be
	one of `iGhostVTProtocol.clientPaths`, root-owned) and permission to look
	the daemon's mach service up. It draws nothing, so it needs none of the
	app's GPU IOKit list; it owns no container, so none of the storage keys;
	it spawns nothing, so nothing the daemon carries.

	`com.apple.private.security.no-sandbox` is deliberately absent. The app
	needs it because FrontBoard launches an app bundle into a container
	profile; this program is exec'd by a shell — the daemon's own sessions or
	sshd, neither of them sandboxed — and inherits no profile to be excepted
	from. If a device ever logs `deny(1) mach-lookup wiki.qaq.ighostvt.service`
	for it, add the key here and relax the matching assertion in
	Scripts/package-deb.sh in the same change.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>wiki.qaq.ighostvt.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.exception.mach-lookup.global-name</key>
	<array>
		<string>wiki.qaq.ighostvt.service</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
